---
description: Dockerfile guidelines — pinned minimal base, multi-stage, non-root.
globs: **/Dockerfile,**/Dockerfile.*,**/*.dockerfile,**/Containerfile
alwaysApply: false
---

- Pin base images to a digest (`@sha256:...`) for prod; prefer minimal (`-slim`, distroless, chainguard, ubi-minimal). NEVER `:latest` or `FROM ubuntu` for app runtime.
- Multi-stage build: `FROM ... AS builder` → final stage copies only the artifact + runtime deps. Cache: lockfile → install → source.
- NEVER `apt-get upgrade`; use `apt-get install --no-install-recommends` and clean `/var/lib/apt/lists/*` in the same `RUN`. NEVER `COPY . .` without a `.dockerignore` excluding `.git`, `.env`, `node_modules`, `__pycache__`.
- Final image MUST run as non-root (`USER <name>`). Set `WORKDIR`. Use exec-form `ENTRYPOINT ["..."]` so SIGTERM reaches the process. Add `HEALTHCHECK` for long-running services.
